            <div xml:id="d501">

                <pb facs="0652" n="553" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg553"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.5216/25: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in El Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Fisher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-11-08T15:00:00-06:00">November 8, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. With reference to my despatch 827, October 15th,<anchor n="90"
                        xml:id="d501-f1"/> Diego Buigas, who resigned as Spanish Chargé d’Affaires
                    ad interim here to support the revolution, informs me that the Salvadoran
                    Government this morning recognized the Burgos Government and extended
                    recognition to him as Chargé.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fisher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
